<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icbb8b8a30d86fe7c9e7f18033a4fd256ef0d297b" commit="27c198b78a202ab4c69cd47f3371ca27e6317b10" commit_message="Make sure the drumroll gesture doesn't hang  Previously, the drumroll gesture was observed hanging sometimes when the finger couldn't quite extend as far as it needed to.  This was always just an issue of tolerances, and not really because the finger wasn't touching the pad.  This CL fixes this issue, making sure that the robot doesn't hang, preventing the rest of the test to run.  This CL fixes the issue by having the robot extend the first finger blindly and record when it came in contact with the pad.  Then it uses that value from then on to have faster taps still.  So in the end the first tap is slightly slower, but all the following ones are the same speed as before, which are the ones that really need to be fast anyway.  BUG=none TEST=manually tested using a DUT/config that would hang.  With this change everything went smoothly and without a hitch  Change-Id: Icbb8b8a30d86fe7c9e7f18033a4fd256ef0d297b Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/326371 Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="326371" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/71/326371/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6d21167ce3d773c9616abd4a728247a1934b96d6" commit="d7dad18f809cf735ae660947e94fb5eaaa3c0128" commit_message="gaia, mediatek, rockchip, tegra: No more disabling key scanning in power files  In http://crosreview.com/28402 code was added to power/gaia.c that disabled keyboard scanning if the power button was pressed.  The purpose, according to that change, was to prevent accidental reboots by pressing the power button together with another key that wasn't the &quot;Refresh&quot; key (specifically: LCtrl, Tab, Reload, t, [, ], y, Dim Screen and Mute).  At the time the original code was added, there was already code in the power button interrupt handler to accomplish the same purpose: see commit 29d25d807c18 (&quot;Keyboard scan must stop driving columns when power button is pressed.&quot;).  It's unclear if the code in the interrupt handler didn't work or if there was some other bug with it.  ...or if perhaps the changes in &quot;gaia/power.c&quot; weren't actually needed and the important part of the original change was the mutex added to the scanning task.  In any case, current testing indicates that the code in power/gaia.c, power/rockchip.c, and power/tegra.c isn't needed anymore.  I ran through the test sequence described in the original CL on my veyron_jerry and I don't see any accidental reboots.  It's also instructive to note that only ARM boards (all presumably copied from gaia) have this extra code.  Presumably if the code was actually needed then x86 boards would also need it.  In any case, let's remove it.  It's suspected that there's some crazy race where the disable in power/rockchip.c is overriding the enable in the main power key handling code and leaving the keyboard disabled.  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:48470 TEST=Same test as CL:28402  Change-Id: I6d21167ce3d773c9616abd4a728247a1934b96d6 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327843 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit dfae7e7ad45f4ce0e8f820caaa05a8754bba0250) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328013 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328013" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/13/328013/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibff5a33d9298b97c58c8aa78bacf4cd711df1d94" commit="9009ae19a3e982f7813ce755183f4b95a67df379" commit_message="dts: Rename boot-stub to coreboot on all boards  cbfstool is now looking for the FMAP section &quot;COREBOOT&quot; when you're not specifying a section explicitly.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=cbfstool &lt;image&gt; print works again for affected boards  Signed-off-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ibff5a33d9298b97c58c8aa78bacf4cd711df1d94 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317263 Commit-Ready: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317263" owner_email="reinauer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/63/317263/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7938.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>